## Self-inflicted false failure, diagnosed and fixed

First version of the new "does NOT call _endGuidedTopicTeaching()" test
failed against the FIXED source, because my own inline source comment in
orb-widget.js literally contained the substring "_endGuidedTopicTeaching():"
(with trailing paren), matching the test's /_endGuidedTopicTeaching\(/
regex. Not a real function call — a false failure caused by my own
comment wording.

Fix: reworded the source comment to "Deliberately does NOT use the
guided-topic completion teardown:" (removing the literal
"_endGuidedTopicTeaching(" substring).

$ npx jest test/frontend/orb-widget-background-watchdog.test.ts
PASS — Test Suites: 1 passed, 1 total / Tests: 8 passed, 8 total

